commit 7a37cdb1ad9d79c4253d8d31d2d1b0c4bca2e447
Author:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
AuthorDate: Thu Jun 18 16:42:51 2026 -0400
Commit:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
CommitDate: Thu Jun 18 16:42:51 2026 -0400

    Bug 2046384 - Remove nsISmtpUrl and nsIMailtoUrl XPCOM interfaces. r=mkmelin

    These interfaces were largely vestigial: nsISmtpUrl's 13 attributes had
    zero consumers in the production code (only its two port constants were
    referenced), and nsIMailtoUrl was only used as a parsing wrapper in one
    place (nsMsgComposeService::GetParamsForMailto).

    Changes:
    - Extract mailto: URL parsing from nsMailtoUrl::ParseMailtoUrl into a
      standalone ParseMailtoSpec() utility in nsMsgComposeService.cpp.
    - Rewrite GetParamsForMailto to use the new parser directly instead of
      creating an intermediate nsMailtoUrl + QI to nsIMailtoUrl.
    - Remove nsISmtpUrl and nsIMailtoUrl interfaces from nsISmtpUrl.idl,
      delete the .idl file entirely.
    - Remove nsSmtpUrl and nsMailtoUrl classes (nsSmtpUrl.h/.cpp).
      from=, followup-to=, organization=, reply-to= and priority= are
      intentionally ignored for security and privacy reasons. Added a
      negative test verifying these parameters do not leak into compose
      fields.
    - Update nsNewMailnewsURI to create nsMsgMailNewsUrl for smtp:/smtps:
      and nsSimpleURI for mailto: instead of the removed classes.
    - Remove component registrations for both classes from components.conf.
    - Inline DEFAULT_SMTP_PORT (25) and DEFAULT_SMTPS_PORT (465) constants
      into SMTPProtocolHandler.sys.mjs and test_smtpProtocols.js.
    - Remove dead #include from nsMsgSendLater.cpp.
    - Rewrite test_mailtoURL.js to test via getParamsForMailto() instead of
      QI to nsIMailtoUrl.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305838

